                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "- when i first started playing this, and got hit with the first cutscene, i was like \"that is really well animated\" then i got to the second quest, and it was the EXACT same cutscene. \n\n- The game only has 3 quests, the quests are definitely unique, but are short.\n\n- it is impossible to walk in a straight line on keyboard, its not debilitating, but it is a nuisance.\n\n+ enemy's are legitimately varied, despite what others might tell you, each area has its own unique enemy set, and each enemy type has a unique ability. I also encountered elites which could be very difficult to kill depending on circumstance.\n\n- sometimes lifespamming is the only way to move forwards, especially on the final boss of quest 3, which is completely impossible to dodge.\n\n- i didnt even get any of the other weapons until beating the game.\n\n+ combat was legitimately fun, i ran crossbow the entire time, and apart from some parts literally being impossible, dodging enemies, doing parkour, and landing precision strikes was enjoy\n\nHonestly, im surprised this game has so many negative reviews, for the most part it isnt a bad game, even with its many flaws, its just extremely overpriced, this is a 3$ game being listed as a 20$ game.",
